  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Thursday)\nIssued at 130 PM CDT Fri Jul 3 2026\n\nRidging continues to build just to the west of our area through the \nextended forecast. As a result, temperatures in the mid-to-upper 90s \nto a few degrees above the century mark can be expected from Sunday \nthrough the end of the period. Rain chances in the 10-30% range are \nmaintained for the western higher terrain (mainly the Davis \nMountains) most days in the extended thanks to upslope flow. Chances \nelsewhere have continued to trend lower thanks to subsidence from \nthe ridge. However, disturbances in the northeasterly flow aloft \nallow for very low evening rain chances (10-20%) to persist in \nnorthernmost and easternmost portions of our area at least early \nnext week. The main difference between this forecast package and the \nprevious one is that highs have trended a degree or two warmer most \ndays thanks to a slight eastward expansion of the ridge/an increase \nin thicknesses over the area.\n\nSprang",
